// What does ! mean?
// this.Vehicles.get(vid)!

// The ! is TypeScript's non-null assertion operator.
// Map.get() can return undefined:
// this.Vehicles.get(vid)

// has a type roughly like:
// Vehicle | undefined

// You're telling TypeScript:
// "I guarantee this vehicle exists. Don't complain about undefined."

// So:
// this.Vehicles.get(vid)!.status

// means:
// Get the vehicle with vid, assume it exists, then access its status.

// ⚠️ If it actually doesn't exist at runtime:
// this.Vehicles.get("wrong-id")!.status

// you can get a runtime error.